      "caption": "The joy was staying parallel, riding alongside.\n\nDAY 10 OF 30 • ACT II: THE GROWING FLAME & SECRET WORLD - Parallel Pedals\n\nThe asphalt stretched open beneath an amber sky. Their cycle tyres hummed together, spinning in easy, effortless rhythm. \"Race me to the junction?\" Isha challenged, wind catching her dupatta like a fluttering sail. \"And let you win?\" Sid grinned, leaning forward over the handlebars. \"You'd lose on purpose anyway, Sid.\"\n\n\"Only to watch you celebrate,\" he laughed, matching her pace stroke for stroke. They rode so close their handlebars nearly brushed, shadows elongating behind them into one single silhouette. Neither rushed ahead. The joy was never about reaching the finish line; it was staying parallel, riding alongside each other.\n\nThis is Day 10 of SIDISHA - Home Was You\nA 30-Day Drabble Collection by Nalkudil Studio\nOne memory. One spark. Every morning 10:15 AM IST.\n\n🔊 Sound on: Roja Janeman (Instrumental Lo-Fi) Â· A.R. Rahman\n\nRead with illustrations on blog - link in bio\nFree 30-Day Booklet: iamsaravofficial.com/book-club\n\nRemember the pure freedom of riding cycles alongside someone until the streetlights came on? 👇\n\n#sidisha #homewasyou #drabble #90slovestory #nalkudilstudio",
