      "caption": "The skies are different. The gravity stays the same.\n\nDAY 22 OF 30 • ACT III: THE THRESHOLD & THE PROMISE - Different Envelopes\n\nTwo white courier envelopes lay open between them on the terrace parapet. Her letter read Delhi. His letter read Bangalore. A gust of dry evening wind ruffled the glossy admission letters, threatening to blow them away. Sid reached out, pressing his palm flat against hers instead of the paper.\n\n\"Two different skies,\" Isha said softly, her voice cracking under the silence of the twilight sky. \"The skies are different, Isha,\" Sid replied, his jaw tense with quiet resolve. \"The gravity pulling us together stays the exact same.\" She nodded through rising tears, but distance was already beginning to breathe.\n\nThis is Day 22 of SIDISHA - Home Was You\nA 30-Day Drabble Collection by Nalkudil Studio\nOne memory. One spark. Every morning 10:15 AM IST.\n\n🔊 Sound on: Tum Ho (Rockstar Acoustic) Â· Mohit Chauhan / A.R. Rahman\n\nRead with illustrations on blog - link in bio\nFree 30-Day Booklet: iamsaravofficial.com/book-club\n\nDid distance ever test a connection that felt destined? How did you survive it? 👇\n\n#sidisha #homewasyou #drabble #firstlove #nalkudilstudio",
