      "punchline": "\"Distant horizons, zero contact—yet never so alone.\"",
      "caption": "Distant horizons, zero contact—yet never so alone.\n\nDAY 25 OF 30 • ACT IV: THE UNDENIABLE US – MUNICH & HOME WAS YOU - Across Hemispheres\n\nSemester breaks brought no shared cycle rides. Following her father’s permanent relocation, Isha moved to Germany for her undergraduate studies, anchoring her life an entire continent away. College dragged on through endless lecture halls and crowded canteens, yet Sid walked through Bangalore like a ghost.\n\nEvery girl with a messily pinned bun made his heart skip a cruel, false beat. Half a world away, shivering in Munich’s unfamiliar snow, Isha tucked Sid’s glowing sketch under her dorm pillow. Separate universities, distant horizons, zero contact—yet neither had ever felt so brutally, irrevocably alone.\n\nThis is Day 25 of SIDISHA - Home Was You\nA 30-Day Drabble Collection by Nalkudil Studio\nOne memory. One spark. Every morning 10:15 AM IST.\n\n🔊 Sound on: Autumn in Munich / River Flows in You Â· Yiruma (Piano)\n\nRead with illustrations on blog - link in bio\nFree 30-Day Booklet: iamsaravofficial.com/book-club\n\n7 years apart across different continents. Do you believe true love ever actually fades? 👇\n\n#sidisha #homewasyou #drabble #lovestory #nalkudilstudio",
